# operating characteristics of the v1 success criteria (two-sided 95% Clopper-Pearson)
# principle: P(pass | sound) >= 0.9, P(pass | doubled nominal error) <= 0.05;
# S1, a conjunction over the key null conditions, meets it as a whole

## Nominal rates (errors by cause, decided 2026-10-08)
  false SUPPORTED 0.025 (alpha/2: the effect test is two-sided at alpha, the direction checked
  afterwards); false NOT SUPPORTED (metric invalid, GATE 4/5) on a valid metric 0.1 (2 alpha:
  GATE 4's upper bound below delta_min alpha/2, GATE 5's negative control alpha, a silent positive
  control shown blind alpha/2); false NO DETECTABLE EFFECT 0.05 (alpha, the TOST's size). A card's nominal
  error is the sum over the routes open on it (panel.allowed); S4 uses the cards' mean. Decisiveness:
  0.85 correct definite outcomes on establishable cards (the oracle reaches >= 0.9), doubled shortfall 0.70.

## S1 as a whole: the number of datasets per key condition (5 conditions)
  the rule first holds at n = 763; k* moves in steps, so it fails again at n = 769-785, 802-808 (up to 1000); the plan's 790 meets it
  S1 false SUPPORTED, key null conditions: 5 conditions x n = 790, each passes with at most 29/790 false SUPPORTED (upper 95% CP bound <= 0.0523); P(one passes | 0.025) = 0.9824, P(all 5 pass | 0.025) = 0.9151, P(a condition passes | 0.050 there) = 0.0465 — meets the principle

